      {
        "id": 65791,
        "name": "TheJayMann",
        "username": "TheJayMann",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-16T18:29:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Regarding the Limited cards, I believe I remember a conversation (which may have been verbal and thus not searchable) in which Christopher said that a player never even has the option to  play a limited card in the first place. If a player is to play a card, any Limited card in hand with a same name in play is considered to not even be in the hand to begin with, not allowing the play. Only cards which would force a play can ever have a second limited card to come into play, which then would trigger the rules which says to instead place it in the trash, unless the card says what to do with the card (such as Atlantian Font of Power). If a card allows ‘random’ cards to be revealed, and playing/putting into play the cards is one of the options allowed (such as Timeshift power), then the play/put into play option is no longer a valid option for a duplicate Limited card.<br>\nNow, this is based ob information a year (possible a year and a half) old, and thus could be irrelevant now.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:43:18.841Z",
