      {
        "id": 65795,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-17T13:58:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Actually, Targeting Entering play and Card Entering play would trigger at different points. As when a card enters play the card isn't doing anything the moment it enters play, it would essentially be a blank card, infact put it upside down while everything that triggers on a \"card entering play\" has been established. Where when a target enteres play it has to be rightside up, allowing the effects on the card to be triggered.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:43:19.122Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
